<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
   FIX: previously no networkSecurityConfig existed at all — meaning
   cleartext (http://) traffic was governed only by Android's own
   platform default (blocked since API 28, allowed on older devices),
   never something this app explicitly decided and documented itself.
   This makes that policy explicit rather than implicit.

   Only affects the STANDARD Android networking stack — OkHttp (TMDB/
   OMDB/OpenSubtitles/SubDL/IntroDB API calls), WebView (the subtitle website
   fallback), HttpURLConnection. Does NOT affect SMB — SmbDataSource/
   SmbVideoScanner talk to jcifs-ng directly over raw sockets, which is
   a separate protocol implementation entirely outside Android's HTTP(S)
   stack and this config's scope. SMB's own protection (message signing)
   is unrelated and unaffected either way.

   The manifest's http:// intent-filters (for "Open with CineVault" on
   direct stream links) were already non-functional for actual playback
   under Android's own default cleartext blocking on modern devices —
   this doesn't change that behavior, just makes it an explicit,
   intentional app policy instead of an implicit platform default.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" />
</network-security-config>
